{"id":14114,"artist":"H De Koning","title":"Yellow rose of Texas","lyrics_plain":"There's a yellow rose in Texas,\nI'm going there to see.\nI know she's waiting for me,\nnobody only me.\nShe cried so when I left her,\nit like to broke her heart.\nAnd if we ever meet again,\nwe never more shall part.\nShe's the sweetest little rosebud,\nthat Texas ever knew.\nHer eyes are bright as diamonds,\nthey sparkle like the dew.\nYou may talk about your Clementine,\nand sing of Rosy Lee,\nBut the yellow rose of Texas,\nis the only one for me.\nOh, I'm going back to find her,\nmy heart is full of woe.\nWe'll sing the songs together,\nthat we sang so long ago.\nI'll pick the banjo gaily,\nand sing the songs of yore.\nThe Yellow Rose of Texas,\nshall be mine forever more.\nThe Yellow Rose of Texas,\nshall be mine forever more.\nThe Yellow Rose of Texas,\nshall be mine forever more.","lyrics_synced":"[00:01.91] There's a yellow rose in Texas,\n[00:04.09] I'm going there to see.\n[00:06.27] I know she's waiting for me,\n[00:08.45] nobody only me.\n[00:10.64] She cried so when I left her,\n[00:12.82] it like to broke her heart.\n[00:15.00] And if we ever meet again,\n[00:17.18] we never more shall part.\n[00:39.00] She's the sweetest little rosebud,\n[00:41.18] that Texas ever knew.\n[00:43.36] Her eyes are bright as diamonds,\n[00:45.55] they sparkle like the dew.\n[00:47.73] You may talk about your Clementine,\n[00:49.91] and sing of Rosy Lee,\n[00:52.09] But the yellow rose of Texas,\n[00:54.00] is the only one for me.\n[00:59.73] Oh, I'm going back to find her,\n[01:01.33] my heart is full of woe.\n[01:02.93] We'll sing the songs together,\n[01:04.53] that we sang so long ago.\n[01:06.13] I'll pick the banjo gaily,\n[01:07.73] and sing the songs of yore.\n[01:09.33] The Yellow Rose of Texas,\n[01:10.73] shall be mine forever more.\n[01:12.53] The Yellow Rose of Texas,\n[01:13.93] shall be mine forever more.\n[01:15.73] The Yellow Rose of Texas,\n[01:17.13] shall be mine forever 